# The old address, sent to the new one.
#
# Setting a primary domain in Netlify does not reliably redirect Netlify's own
# *.netlify.app subdomain, so artiumm.netlify.app kept serving the whole app —
# a second live copy of the site, on an origin whose localStorage, session and
# service worker are all separate from the real one. Somebody could stay signed
# in there indefinitely and never see the domain everyone else is using.
#
# The trailing ! forces the rule even though a file matches the path, which is
# needed here: without it index.html is served for / before the rule is reached.
#
# Deploy previews (deploy-preview-N--artiumm.netlify.app) do not match this
# host and keep working normally.
https://artiumm.netlify.app/*   https://art-ium.com/:splat   301!
http://artiumm.netlify.app/*    https://art-ium.com/:splat   301!

# Everything else is the single-page app. Screens are state-based today, so
# nothing depends on this yet — it is here so that the first real route added
# does not 404 on a hard refresh.
/*                              /index.html                  200
